Z||000009||Seanh||11-13-2000||11:13 PM||||How, and what program are you useing to do that? I really like that effect. I use PSP 6.0 and I have to just erase real nicely around the edge of the objects I want, and even then I cant seem to get the background transparent. Thanks<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig2.gif">     <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jaei Sun||11-14-2000||12:07 AM||||I use PSP as well... I just upgraded to 7 but it's basically the same for both.<P>This works just like a Hollywood Blue Screen<P>- Use the Freehand Selection tool to outline your car (or what ever you're working on). <P>- And then under Selections click Invert.<P>- Next select a background color that is outragous! Like lime green or bright blue.  Then Hit the "Del" button on the keyboard.  <P>- Under Colors choose "Select Palette Transparency. This reduces the colors to 256 and then allows you to choose a color that will the the color that is transparent in web browsers.<P>- Select the color that you choose as the outragous color.<P>- Don't forget to save as a gif!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/umebottle3/fie_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
